> Empty rules require both arrival orders

Use S→A B, A→ε and B→A with an empty input. A can complete before
B→.A is predicted. When that later item begins waiting for A, simply
processing A's old completion once is insufficient. The waiter must
notice the already completed zero-width span and advance immediately.

The earlier implementation also iterated a column's vector by reference
while nullable completion appended to the same vector. A compiled
old-header sanitizer probe reproduces a heap-use-after-free. The new
kernel copies the current item before inserting, indexes processed
waiters, and remembers the first completed span. It joins either when
the span finishes or when a later zero-width waiter arrives. No borrowed
item reference survives insertion.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/earley_nullable.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::ContextFreeGrammar g{{{"S",{"A","B"}},{"A",{}},{"B",{"A"}}},"S"};
  const auto t=dm::algorithms::earley_trace(g,{});dm::algorithms::EarleyLocation selected;
  std::print("Nullable empty word: accepted {}; items {}; completion joins {}; late nullable joins {}; capture entries {}.\n\n",t.accepted,t.work.unique_items,t.work.completion_joins,t.work.nullable_joins,t.captured_entries);
  std::print("| item ordinal | actual item in column zero |\n| ---: | :--- |\n");
  for(std::size_t i=0;i<t.chart[0].size();++i){std::print("| {} | {} |\n",i,dm::algorithms::earley_item_text(t,{0,i}));const auto r=t.reasons[0][i];
    if(r.action==dm::algorithms::EarleyAction::complete&&r.first.column==r.second.column&&r.first.index>r.second.index)selected={0,i};}
  if(selected.column==dm::algorithms::earley_no_item)throw std::runtime_error("missing actual late nullable join");
  const auto cause=t.reasons[selected.column][selected.index];
  std::print("\nLate completion: waiter ({},{}), earlier completed span ({},{}), target ({},{}).\n",cause.first.column,cause.first.index,cause.second.column,cause.second.index,selected.column,selected.index);
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(64,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.6;box.height=1.6;box.font_size=23;
  d.node("waiter",{0,0},std::format("waiter ({},{})\n{}",cause.first.column,cause.first.index,dm::algorithms::earley_item_text(t,cause.first)),box);
  box.fill={187,247,208};d.node("finished",{6,0},std::format("already completed ({},{})\n{}",cause.second.column,cause.second.index,dm::algorithms::earley_item_text(t,cause.second)),box);
  box.fill={254,215,170};d.node("joined",{3,-3.7},std::format("new item ({},{})\n{}",selected.column,selected.index,dm::algorithms::earley_item_text(t,selected)),box)
   .edge("waiter","joined","advance").edge("finished","joined","reuse empty A")
   .text({3,2.4},"A completed before B began waiting",26).save_svg("build/earley_nullable.svg");
}
