\alttext(A native diagram combines the later B waiter with an already completed empty A and shows their actual newly inserted B item.)

The same closure handles unit cycles and S→SS|ε|a without an infinite
search. It recognizes language membership; it does not enumerate all
parses. Even the epsilon-free S→SS|a has five binary parses for four a
leaves: splitting the root gives 1·2+1·1+2·1=5. Several derivations
can therefore share one item. First-insertion reasons record one sound
way each item arrived, not every derivation that could justify it.

> Derive two exact growth families

For the original accepted word a^k b^k, N=2k. Its column sizes are
2 initially, four at each a, two at each nonfinal b, and one at the
end. Thus I=6k+1=3N+1 unique items. Every inner completed S has one
outer waiter, while the root has none, giving k−1 completion joins.
This particular family is linear; a bounded count in this plot does
not establish a general bound for every grammar.

For S→SS|a on a^N, every positive substring is an S. At boundary j
there are j completed items, j items after their first S, and two
predicted items, for 2j+2 items. Consequently

\[
I=\sum_{j=0}^{N}(2j+2)=(N+1)(N+2).
\]

At origin j there are j+1 waiters for S, and N−j nonempty S spans
can finish later. Each waiter/span pair is joined once, giving

\[
J=\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}(j+1)(N-j)=\frac{N(N+1)(N+2)}{6}.
\]

The next program checks those formulas against actual retained-item
and join counters. The panels plot logical operation counts, not CPU
time, and no counter measures the number of parse trees.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/earley_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::ContextFreeGrammar balanced{{{"S",{"a","S","b"}},{"S",{"a","b"}}},"S"};
  const dm::algorithms::ContextFreeGrammar ambiguous{{{"S",{"S","S"}},{"S",{"a"}}},"S"};
  std::vector<double>x,linear,quadratic,cubic;
  std::print("| tokens N | balanced items | balanced joins | ambiguous items | exact item formula | ambiguous joins | exact join formula |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t n:{4,8,16,32,64,128}){std::vector<std::string> word(n/2,"a");word.insert(word.end(),n/2,"b");
    const auto a=dm::algorithms::earley_recognize_work(balanced,word),b=dm::algorithms::earley_recognize_work(ambiguous,std::vector<std::string>(n,"a"));
    const auto exact_items=(n+1)*(n+2),exact_joins=n*(n+1)*(n+2)/6;
    if(!a.accepted||!b.accepted||a.work.unique_items!=3*n+1||a.work.completion_joins!=n/2-1||b.work.unique_items!=exact_items||b.work.completion_joins!=exact_joins)throw std::runtime_error("growth identity failed");
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,a.work.unique_items,a.work.completion_joins,b.work.unique_items,exact_items,b.work.completion_joins,exact_joins);
    x.push_back(std::log2(n));linear.push_back(std::log2(a.work.unique_items));quadratic.push_back(std::log2(b.work.unique_items));cubic.push_back(std::log2(b.work.completion_joins));
  }
  auto a=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();a.line(x,linear,"balanced",{22,163,74}).points(x,linear,"",{22,163,74},5)
   .line(x,quadratic,"ambiguous",{37,99,235}).points(x,quadratic,"",{37,99,235},5)
   .title("Unique chart items: linear versus quadratic").x_label("log2(tokens)").y_label("log2(actual unique items)").y_limits(0,19);
  auto b=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();b.line(x,cubic,"joins",{220,38,38}).points(x,cubic,"",{220,38,38},5)
   .title("Ambiguous grammar: cubic waiter/span joins").x_label("log2(tokens)").y_label("log2(actual completion joins)").y_limits(0,23);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(a).add(b).size(1100,550).title("Exact family counts verify different chart and completion growth")
   .fit_panels().save_svg("build/earley_work.svg");
}
