> Capture budgets and precise token semantics

A trace owns its grammar, tokens, actual chart and parallel first reasons.
Its base cost is 2N+P+sum(rhs lengths)+2 logical records: start/LHS/RHS
symbol strings, token strings and one metadata record per chart boundary.
Each new unique item and first reason add two records. String bytes,
runtime hash indexes, scalar fields and allocator overhead are excluded.
The default cap is one million; zero disables only that optional quota.
Raw geometry and the base cap are checked before copying or column
allocation. Each further unique insertion is checked online; duplicate
attempts consume no capture entries. Failure returns no partial trace.

The original eight-token chart therefore costs 25 base records plus
2·25 item/reason records, exactly 75. A one-short budget fails even
though the grammar is valid. Counts, production/dot/origin indices and
legacy int column sizes have mandatory representability checks.

Symbols are opaque names. An empty RHS derives an empty word, while a
RHS containing the one empty string names a terminal and consumes one
atomic token. Empty strings, embedded NUL and UTF-8 symbol names remain
valid; tokenization is the caller's responsibility. The selected-item
formatter escapes control bytes and checks its local coordinates. It
does not certify every field of a caller-edited trace.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/earley_boundaries.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const dm::algorithms::ContextFreeGrammar g{{{"S",{"a","S","b"}},{"S",{"a","b"}}},"S"};
  const std::vector<std::string> word{"a","a","a","a","b","b","b","b"};
  const auto exact=dm::algorithms::earley_trace(g,word,75),disabled=dm::algorithms::earley_trace(g,word,0);int caps=0,indices=0,format=0;
  for(std::size_t limit:{24,74})try{(void)dm::algorithms::earley_trace(g,word,limit);}catch(const std::length_error&){++caps;}
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::earley_trace_base_entries(g,static_cast<std::size_t>(std::numeric_limits<int>::max())+1);}catch(const std::length_error&){++indices;}
  auto edited=exact;edited.chart[0][0].dot=99;
  try{(void)dm::algorithms::earley_item_text(edited,{0,0});}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++format;}
  std::print("Exact entries {}; disabled-cap entries {}; expected base/one-short rejections {}/2; index rejection {}/1; edited-item rejection {}/1.\n",exact.captured_entries,disabled.captured_entries,caps,indices,format);
  const dm::algorithms::ContextFreeGrammar epsilon{{{"S",{}}},"S"},named{{{"S",{""}}},"S"};
  const auto e=dm::algorithms::earley_trace(epsilon,{}),zero=dm::algorithms::earley_trace(named,{}),one=dm::algorithms::earley_trace(named,{""});
  std::print("Empty RHS on empty word: {}; one empty-named terminal on empty word: {}; on one empty-named token: {}.\n",e.accepted,zero.accepted,one.accepted);
  const std::string nul(1,'\0');const dm::algorithms::ContextFreeGrammar bytes{{{"S",{"id",nul}}},"S"};
  std::print("Atomic id/NUL tokens accepted {}; split i/d/NUL tokens accepted {}; undefined start accepted {}.\n",dm::algorithms::earley_recognize(bytes,{"id",nul}),dm::algorithms::earley_recognize(bytes,{"i","d",nul}),dm::algorithms::earley_recognize({},{}));
  dm::graphics::Diagram d(64,1100);dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;box.width=4.8;box.height=2;box.font_size=23;
  box.fill={187,247,208};d.node("epsilon",{0,0},std::format("{}\ninput []\naccepted {}",dm::algorithms::earley_item_text(e,{0,0}),e.accepted),box);
  box.fill={254,215,170};d.node("zero",{5.8,0},std::format("{}\ninput []\naccepted {}",dm::algorithms::earley_item_text(zero,{0,0}),zero.accepted),box);
  box.fill={187,247,208};d.node("one",{11.6,0},std::format("{}\ninput [\"\"]\naccepted {}",dm::algorithms::earley_item_text(one,{1,0}),one.accepted),box)
   .text({5.8,2.6},"Empty RHS and an empty-named token have different meanings",26).save_svg("build/earley_boundaries.svg");
}
